-- title:
--   Rigidity of Hecke tower data with equal divisor correspondences
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $q,q'$ and let $F_0$ be a field over $K=\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is a curve over $K$ in the project's sense: principal divisors exist, every place has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega_{F_0/K}$ is free of rank one. Let $\mathbb T,\mathbb T'$ be two pieces of tower data for $(q,q',F_0)$, each consisting of a family of fields $F_\ell$ indexed by the primes $\ell\neq q,q'$, each a curve over $K$ and essentially of finite type over $K$, together with $K$-algebra maps $\varphi_{\ell,i}:F_0\to F_\ell$ for $i\in\{0,1\}$ that are integral and finite along. Assume first that at every $\ell$ the two data induce the same correspondence on divisors of $F_0$: for every divisor $D$ (a finitely supported $\mathbb Z$-valued function on places of $F_0$), the pushforward along $\varphi_{\ell,1}$ of the pullback along $\varphi_{\ell,0}$ of $D$ agrees with the same construction for $\mathbb T'$. Assume second that $\mathbb T'$ is generated: for every $\ell$ the subfield of $\mathbb T'.F_\ell$ generated by the union of the images of $\varphi'_{\ell,0}$ and $\varphi'_{\ell,1}$ is the whole field; no such hypothesis is imposed on $\mathbb T$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a family of $K$-algebra isomorphisms $\theta_\ell:\mathbb T.F_\ell\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\mathbb T'.F_\ell$ with two properties. First, $\theta_\ell(\varphi_{\ell,i}(x))=\varphi'_{\ell,i}(x)$ for all $i\in\{0,1\}$ and $x\in F_0$. Second, $\theta$ transports semilinear symmetries: for every index type $S$, every $g_0:S\to\mathrm{SemilinearAut}(K,F_0)$ (pairs consisting of a ring automorphism of the field and one of $K$, compatible with the structure map, acting by the pointwise scalar action) and every pair of families $g_\ell,g'_\ell:S\to\mathrm{SemilinearAut}(K,\mathbb T.F_\ell)$, resp. $\mathrm{SemilinearAut}(K,\mathbb T'.F_\ell)$, such that $g_\ell(\sigma)\cdot\varphi_{\ell,i}(x)=\varphi_{\ell,i}(g_0(\sigma)\cdot x)$ and $g'_\ell(\sigma)\cdot\varphi'_{\ell,i}(x)=\varphi'_{\ell,i}(g_0(\sigma)\cdot x)$ for all arrows, all $\sigma\in S$ and all $x\in F_0$, one has $\theta_\ell(g_\ell(\sigma)\cdot y)=g'_\ell(\sigma)\cdot\theta_\ell(y)$ for all $\ell$, $\sigma$ and $y\in\mathbb T.F_\ell$.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement for Hecke tower data: the two degeneracy maps at each level are determined, up to a unique isomorphism of levels, by the correspondence they induce on divisors of the base curve, provided the target tower is generated by the two images. It is used to replace an abstract tower satisfying the expected Hecke relations by a concrete model, and is cited by the two statements producing descent data intertwining the base in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part, where the second conjunct is applied to Galois actions and to Atkin–Lehner involutions.
